    "result_text": "The three test files are `AcceptanceTest` (the only concrete test class with 2 tests), plus `AcceptanceBase` (abstract) and `AuditLogCapture` (a helper). All tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated the locality derivation to prefer the postcode over the city.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`:\n\n1. Added a `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES` table mapping each region to its inclusive 4-digit range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099).\n\n2. Rewrote `locality(Owner)` to first resolve the region from the owner's postcode via a new `regionForPostcode` helper, and only fall back to the existing `CITY_REGION` city table when the postcode is absent, malformed, or in no known range \u2014 returning `UNKNOWN` when neither resolves.\n\n`regionForPostcode` safely handles null/non-4-digit postcodes (returning `null` to trigger the city fallback), so known cities still map to the same region while cities sharing a name are now disambiguated by postcode.\n\n**Verification** \u2014 the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), including both the pre-existing `coreRegionFromPostcodeRange` case and the new `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` case that proves a VIC-range postcode on an unknown city yields `VIC`.",
